# A divisor that IS the literal zero is decidable by reading, so it is refused
# where it is written rather than left to fail at run time. The guarded case is
# the other half and lives in examples/logical_ops.kso, where `2 < 1 and 1 / 0
# < 9` compiles: `and` is an `if`, a branch may be unreachable, and refusing
# one would refuse a program that runs.
#
# Nothing pinned this half. The refusal moved into the per-node walk in the
# change that added this fixture, carried by a flag that turns off under an
# `if`'s branches, and the whole error corpus stayed byte-identical -- because
# the corpus had no case for it either way.
pub play = print "{10 / 0}"
